## THE DESIGN (decided at source by the drafter; every omission needs your written justification)
1. **RD-456, in `static/js/first-run-setup.js`.** The page remembers the stored AI state from its last SUCCESSFUL read of `/api/setup/ai-model` (the `aiState` field; null before any read and after a failed read). `_aoaiPayloadFromForm()` adds `aiEnabled: true` ONLY when the remembered state is the string `not-set-up` (the skip-then-configure path above); in every other case, including unknown, the key is ABSENT from the body (not false, not null). After a save the server answers `aiEnabled` (`backend/server.js:16788`): when that answer is `true` the remembered state becomes `on`; otherwise it is left as it was. The connection test (`testAoaiConfig`) builds its body from the same function and the server ignores `aiEnabled` there (no `req.body.aiEnabled` read in that route), so its behaviour does not change. The other four body keys are byte-identical to today's in every state. **Reasoning to carry into READY:** stored on, never set and administrator-off all keep their stored value; skipped plus a new configuration turns AI on exactly as today; a read that failed leaves the stored value alone (the safe side).
2. **RD-492, same file.** In the success branch the two `enforce-auth-card` statements become a guarded lookup: if the card is absent nothing is painted and nothing throws; if it were present the same two style writes run as today. Do NOT add an element to `first-run-setup.html`, do not change a colour, and do not touch the button's own success styling at `:4133-4134`. The success box, its text and the banner refresh stay as they are.
3. **RD-808, same file.** `:383` becomes `.replace(/\/$/, '')` (one trailing slash removed, nothing else), no other change to that expression.
4. **RD-475 and RD-560, `static/login.html`.** The one `integrity` value on the Bootstrap Icons 1.10.0 link at `:10` becomes `sha384-l4UPAMHGzl7zwogLW4nOwaU2XTk6oiM1jhCRQstZEndoIiA2I5bg6fST3wzBSRBD`, character for character the value `static/index.html:13` carries (print both by `grep -o` and `cmp`); nothing else on the line changes. This is a VISIBLE change (four icons appear on the sign-in page, which the ticket's own measurement says were blank): READY lists it with the received evidence, never silently.
5. **RD-481, the two pages.** Every relative `src` and `href` value on `static/login.html` and `static/first-run-setup.html` gets a leading `/` (the property: after the edit a program finds 0 values that are not an absolute URL, an absolute path, `#...`, `mailto:`, `data:` or `javascript:`; and the files differ from BASE ONLY in those attribute values, proved by program, below). The 5 + 18 values are listed in STATE. Do not touch an already-absolute value, an `https://` link or a `#` anchor.
